        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To simplify an expression containing parentheses, we expand the parentheses and then collect like terms. </p>",
            "readable_text": "To simplify an expression containing parentheses, we expand the parentheses and then collect like terms.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>For example, let&#x27;s simplify the following expression: </p>",
            "readable_text": "For example, let's simplify the following expression:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3(x + 2) + 4x]</span> </p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 3(x + 2) + 4x]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Our first step is to distribute the <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3]</span> over each of the terms in the parentheses:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Our first step is to distribute the [MATH: 3] over each of the terms in the parentheses:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\eqalign{\n3(x + 2) + 4x &amp;= \\[5pt]\n3\\cdot x + 3\\cdot 2 + 4x &amp;= \\[5pt]\n(3x) + (6) + 4x &amp;= \\[5pt]\n3x +6 + 4x &amp;\n}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \\eqalign{\n3(x + 2) + 4x &= \\[5pt]\n3\\cdot x + 3\\cdot 2 + 4x &= \\[5pt]\n(3x) + (6) + 4x &= \\[5pt]\n3x +6 + 4x &\n}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>The second and final step is to collect the like terms:</p>",
            "readable_text": "The second and final step is to collect the like terms:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\eqalign{\n3x + 6 + 4x &amp;= \\\n(3x + 4x) + 6 &amp;= \\\n7x + 6\n}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \\eqalign{\n3x + 6 + 4x &= \\\n(3x + 4x) + 6 &= \\\n7x + 6\n}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nTo simplify an expression containing parentheses, we expand the parentheses and then collect like terms.\n\nContent:\nFor example, let's simplify the following expression:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 3(x + 2) + 4x]\n\nContent:\nOur first step is to distribute the [MATH: 3] over each of the terms in the parentheses:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n3(x + 2) + 4x &= \\[5pt]\n3\\cdot x + 3\\cdot 2 + 4x &= \\[5pt]\n(3x) + (6) + 4x &= \\[5pt]\n3x +6 + 4x &\n}]\n\nContent:\nThe second and final step is to collect the like terms:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n3x + 6 + 4x &= \\\n(3x + 4x) + 6 &= \\\n7x + 6\n}]"
      },
